<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine April tax revenue up 20.2 pct vs Apr '96.</title>
<headline>Argentine April tax revenue up 20.2 pct vs Apr '96.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine tax revenue was $3.94 billion in April, up 20.2 percent from April 1996, the Economy Ministry said Friday.</p>
<p>Value-added tax revenue was $1.61 billion, up 8.5 percent from April last year.</p>
<p>Income tax revenue rose by 56.7 percent to $747.6 million.</p>
<p>Total government revenue including contributions to the private pension fund system rose 21.4 percent to $4.23 billion.</p>
<p>((--Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
